1
00:00:28,410 --> 00:00:30,704
Previously on
Dating Alys Perez.

2
00:00:32,518 --> 00:00:33,624
She'll be fine.

3
00:00:33,632 --> 00:00:35,334
I think you have to check on Tripp.

4
00:00:35,351 --> 00:00:37,062
On how he's doing.

5
00:00:37,070 --> 00:00:38,938
Where's Tripp?
Bring me to him.

6
00:00:39,407 --> 00:00:40,256
Come on, Alys.

7
00:00:40,257 --> 00:00:41,717
Take me to Tripp!

8
00:00:41,717 --> 00:00:43,177
Are you deaf or what?!

9
00:00:44,510 --> 00:00:45,553
Alys!

10
00:00:47,617 --> 00:00:50,182
What is that woman doing here?

11
00:00:50,187 --> 00:00:52,039
You almost killed him!

12
00:00:53,039 --> 00:00:55,124
You almost killed my son!

13
00:00:55,634 --> 00:00:57,636
And you killed your own baby?!

14
00:00:57,918 --> 00:00:59,211
What kind of mother are you?!

15
00:01:01,933 --> 00:01:05,728
I always lose something
whenever I choose you.

16
00:01:06,417 --> 00:01:07,584
I hate you!

17
00:01:08,439 --> 00:01:11,776
I don't want you in my life anymore.

18
00:01:12,459 --> 00:01:14,002
Let's end this.

19
00:01:54,057 --> 00:01:55,476
- Ma'am Kat?
- Yes, Ma'am?

20
00:01:55,476 --> 00:01:57,228
Where is the patient staying here?

21
00:01:57,613 --> 00:01:59,461
Weren’t you informed, Ma’am?

22
00:01:59,468 --> 00:02:00,499
About what?

23
00:02:00,515 --> 00:02:01,641
He's gone.

24
00:02:04,425 --> 00:02:05,633
Yes, Ma'am.

25
00:02:05,648 --> 00:02:07,384
It happened recently.

26
00:02:07,390 --> 00:02:08,390
Oh my God.

27
00:02:10,692 --> 00:02:13,236
What happened?
I thought he was recovering.

28
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:16,413
Sorry, Ma'am.

29
00:02:16,421 --> 00:02:19,499
What I meant was good news.

30
00:02:19,507 --> 00:02:22,203
He's gone because he was transferred.

31
00:02:23,288 --> 00:02:24,706
Oh my God!

32
00:02:25,081 --> 00:02:28,113
Ma'am Kat!
You scared me!

33
00:02:28,125 --> 00:02:29,125
Sorry.

34
00:02:30,406 --> 00:02:31,491
Where was he transferred?

35
00:02:31,491 --> 00:02:32,676
Which room?

36
00:02:32,679 --> 00:02:33,722
He isn't here, Ma'am.

37
00:02:33,722 --> 00:02:35,733
He's been moved to another hospital.

38
00:02:35,742 --> 00:02:37,336
Which hospital?

39
00:02:37,343 --> 00:02:39,019
Sorry, Ma'am.
I honestly don't know.

40
00:02:43,273 --> 00:02:44,024
- Please.
- Faster!

41
00:02:44,024 --> 00:02:47,402
I just need to know where
Mr. Palma was transferred.

42
00:02:48,028 --> 00:02:49,071
Ma'am,

43
00:02:49,071 --> 00:02:50,948
I'm sorry.
You're not family.

44
00:02:50,948 --> 00:02:53,659
We cannot disclose
any information to you.

45
00:02:54,118 --> 00:02:56,554
So what if I'm not his immediate family?

46
00:02:56,562 --> 00:02:57,562
I'm his friend.

47
00:02:57,570 --> 00:02:59,905
Am I not allowed to be concerned?

48
00:02:59,914 --> 00:03:02,141
What I'm asking you is simple,

49
00:03:02,156 --> 00:03:04,149
tell me where he was moved!

50
00:03:04,164 --> 00:03:05,469
Ma'am, please calm down.

51
00:03:05,476 --> 00:03:07,319
You've got some nerve
asking me to calm down!

52
00:03:07,328 --> 00:03:10,140
I've been asking calmly the whole time.
Haven't I?

53
00:03:10,148 --> 00:03:11,365
It's useless to keep—

54
00:03:11,367 --> 00:03:13,318
- Ma'am, calm down.
- What the hell?

55
00:03:13,318 --> 00:03:15,320
- Ma'am, calm down.
- Don't fucking touch me!

56
00:03:17,030 --> 00:03:19,123
Just tell me where they transferred him!

57
00:03:19,125 --> 00:03:20,293
Ma'am, I'm sorry.

58
00:03:20,293 --> 00:03:23,588
Again, we cannot release
any information to you.

59
00:03:31,413 --> 00:03:33,248
You can't take him away from me!

60
00:06:50,341 --> 00:06:52,750
What is that woman doing here?!

61
00:06:52,758 --> 00:06:55,117
I left with my son healthy!

62
00:06:55,125 --> 00:06:56,584
And now I returned?

63
00:06:56,584 --> 00:07:00,274
And now he's in a coma with
multiple internal injuries?

64
00:07:00,298 --> 00:07:02,926
You do not deserve to see my son!

65
00:07:04,227 --> 00:07:05,227
But Tripp

66
00:07:07,222 --> 00:07:09,516
I need to see you again.

67
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:12,976
I need to make it up to you.

68
00:08:10,822 --> 00:08:13,449
My baby!

69
00:08:15,840 --> 00:08:18,509
I'm so sorry.

70
00:08:29,831 --> 00:08:32,834
I'm so sorry.

71
00:08:35,339 --> 00:08:36,549
Why?

72
00:08:37,936 --> 00:08:41,231
Why did this have to happen to me?

73
00:08:42,210 --> 00:08:44,921
To the people I love.

74
00:08:47,114 --> 00:08:48,449
Am I cursed?

75
00:08:49,236 --> 00:08:51,113
Do I deserve all of this?

76
00:08:52,150 --> 00:08:55,529
Am I destined to be everyone's burden?

77
00:09:07,115 --> 00:09:08,617
Maybe yes.

78
00:09:09,513 --> 00:09:11,515
Maybe this is all on me.

79
00:09:12,630 --> 00:09:15,223
I'm not just hurting myself.

80
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:18,535
But everyone else who loves me.

81
00:09:19,327 --> 00:09:21,580
I don't deserve them,

82
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:26,001
because all I ever do is hurt them.

83
00:09:26,826 --> 00:09:29,537
I don't deserve to be happy.

84
00:09:41,911 --> 00:09:44,435
I tried to get up.

85
00:09:44,436 --> 00:09:47,063
I tried to put everything right.

86
00:09:48,043 --> 00:09:51,380
But the more I try to fix my mistakes,

87
00:09:52,231 --> 00:09:54,692
the more I hurt people around me.

88
00:09:57,510 --> 00:10:00,304
The more I lose them.

89
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:05,795
Until I don't know if I
have anything left to fight for.

90
00:10:44,740 --> 00:10:46,513
I give up.

91
00:10:47,946 --> 00:10:49,489
I wish I could be numb to all of this.

92
00:10:51,232 --> 00:10:53,082
I just want everything to stop.

93
00:10:54,703 --> 00:10:56,872
To run away from this feeling.

94
00:10:58,732 --> 00:11:00,167
I just want to rest.

95
00:11:12,232 --> 00:11:14,732
You almost killed my son!

96
00:11:14,740 --> 00:11:17,034
And you killed your own baby?!

97
00:11:17,034 --> 00:11:18,703
What kind of mother are you?!

98
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:28,651
I don’t want to do this anymore.

99
00:11:31,247 --> 00:11:33,374
I killed my baby.

100
00:11:34,136 --> 00:11:36,722
I killed my baby.

101
00:11:37,615 --> 00:11:38,951
I don't want to see,

102
00:11:38,958 --> 00:11:39,959
or hear

103
00:11:39,959 --> 00:11:41,291
or feel any of this.

104
00:11:42,670 --> 00:11:45,965
I just want to let go of this weight.

105
00:11:47,205 --> 00:11:49,541
All I want is my peace.

106
00:11:51,509 --> 00:11:54,346
I want my peace.

107
00:12:16,829 --> 00:12:19,123
Mommy, I need help.

108
00:12:22,707 --> 00:12:24,584
I need help, Mommy.

109
00:12:26,213 --> 00:12:28,674
I can't take this anymore.

110
00:12:44,411 --> 00:12:46,913
Three months.

111
00:12:46,913 --> 00:12:49,582
Three months in rehab.

112
00:12:50,643 --> 00:12:53,771
I'm not sure if I'm completely okay.

113
00:12:55,419 --> 00:12:56,545
Maybe yes.

114
00:12:57,372 --> 00:12:58,540
Maybe no.

115
00:12:58,993 --> 00:13:02,413
All I know is I am better.

116
00:13:03,613 --> 00:13:06,991
But the guilt of losing people
still haunts me.

117
00:13:08,538 --> 00:13:11,625
Sometimes I still blame myself.

118
00:13:12,086 --> 00:13:14,255
Sometimes I just want to run.

119
00:13:14,663 --> 00:13:16,122
Leave.

120
00:13:17,457 --> 00:13:20,001
But I don't know where and when.

121
00:13:30,442 --> 00:13:33,570
Thank you for buying my pastry shop, Tofer.

122
00:13:35,302 --> 00:13:36,698
It's nothing, Alys.

123
00:13:37,617 --> 00:13:41,412
It’d be such a waste if your
baby ended up with someone else.

124
00:13:49,718 --> 00:13:52,804
I can't really imagine
anyone running it but you.

125
00:13:55,416 --> 00:13:57,167
I realized...

126
00:13:59,227 --> 00:14:01,605
I needed a clean slate.

127
00:14:02,476 --> 00:14:06,438
That place just held way
too many memories for me.

128
00:14:07,410 --> 00:14:11,206
And maybe it's time that I let it go.

129
00:14:12,102 --> 00:14:13,520
Alys...

130
00:14:14,328 --> 00:14:15,913
You know what?

131
00:14:16,834 --> 00:14:19,962
This is the first time
in a really long time,

132
00:14:20,632 --> 00:14:22,967
that I've made a decision
that's really for me.

133
00:14:26,492 --> 00:14:30,538
Then, I'm so proud of you for that.

134
00:14:33,937 --> 00:14:35,772
Thank you, Tofer.

135
00:14:45,657 --> 00:14:47,033
Tofer?

136
00:14:47,033 --> 00:14:48,451
Hmm?

137
00:14:49,158 --> 00:14:50,826
I'm just curious.

138
00:14:53,375 --> 00:14:56,295
Do you know where Tripp is?

139
00:15:02,893 --> 00:15:04,269
Okay.

140
00:15:37,294 --> 00:15:39,088
Would Kei know?

141
00:16:05,017 --> 00:16:06,347
Hello, Kei?

142
00:16:06,349 --> 00:16:09,638
Alys!
I'm glad you're better.

143
00:16:09,654 --> 00:16:10,654
I miss you.

144
00:16:11,853 --> 00:16:13,607
I miss you too, Kei.

145
00:16:13,615 --> 00:16:15,033
Why’d you call?

146
00:16:18,341 --> 00:16:20,857
I just wanted to ask if you know

147
00:16:20,872 --> 00:16:22,345
where Tripp is.

148
00:16:23,810 --> 00:16:25,177
Alys...

149
00:16:25,193 --> 00:16:28,106
No, I just wanted to know.

150
00:16:29,607 --> 00:16:31,234
I'm sorry, Alys.

151
00:16:31,234 --> 00:16:32,735
I don't know either.

152
00:16:33,820 --> 00:16:34,821
Don't worry.

153
00:16:34,821 --> 00:16:37,699
I’ll call you as soon
as I find out anything.

154
00:16:39,271 --> 00:16:40,647
No worries, Kei.

155
00:16:40,647 --> 00:16:41,732
Thanks.

156
00:16:46,153 --> 00:16:48,113
Who else can I ask?

157
00:17:02,838 --> 00:17:05,507
Alys, maybe he’s still upset with you.

158
00:17:12,316 --> 00:17:15,152
But how will you know if you won't try?

159
00:17:25,176 --> 00:17:26,176
Oh, Alys.

160
00:17:26,860 --> 00:17:28,028
You called?

161
00:17:28,358 --> 00:17:29,818
Hello, Uncle.

162
00:17:31,365 --> 00:17:32,365
How are you coping?

163
00:17:36,768 --> 00:17:38,269
I'm okay.

164
00:17:38,851 --> 00:17:40,853
Compared to 3 months ago.

165
00:17:42,119 --> 00:17:43,328
Good for you.

166
00:17:47,117 --> 00:17:49,161
Uncle...

167
00:17:53,220 --> 00:17:55,722
Have you heard anything about Tripp?

168
00:17:56,932 --> 00:17:58,392
Don't worry about him.

169
00:17:58,392 --> 00:18:00,394
We're hoping he does well in the States.

170
00:18:02,390 --> 00:18:03,390
States?

171
00:18:04,773 --> 00:18:05,941
Uncle?

172
00:18:06,483 --> 00:18:09,194
Alys, he's in California now.

173
00:18:11,242 --> 00:18:12,577
California?

174
00:18:13,156 --> 00:18:14,950
Yes, in a hospital there.

175
00:18:16,952 --> 00:18:18,203
Anyway,

176
00:18:18,203 --> 00:18:19,955
I need to go.
I have a meeting.

177
00:18:20,513 --> 00:18:22,182
Thank you, Uncle.

178
00:18:22,182 --> 00:18:23,433
Thank you so much.

179
00:18:24,642 --> 00:18:25,685
Alys?

180
00:18:25,685 --> 00:18:27,854
Hope you are not blaming yourself.

181
00:18:27,854 --> 00:18:29,689
It was an accident.

182
00:18:29,689 --> 00:18:30,689
Okay?

183
00:18:33,044 --> 00:18:34,045
Okay, Uncle.

184
00:18:47,410 --> 00:18:48,953
California.

185
00:18:49,646 --> 00:18:51,396
This is my sign.

186
00:18:52,904 --> 00:18:55,725
I was looking for a where and a when.

187
00:18:55,732 --> 00:18:58,026
I don't know where Tripp is but

188
00:18:58,026 --> 00:19:01,613
now I know where to start.

189
00:19:12,794 --> 00:19:15,005
For the longest time,

190
00:19:15,005 --> 00:19:18,925
I thought my life stopped,
the day my world fell apart.

191
00:19:21,532 --> 00:19:23,367
Why aren't you answering me?

192
00:19:27,946 --> 00:19:30,157
Where are you, Bestie?

193
00:19:30,937 --> 00:19:34,315
I thought I'd carry the guilt forever.

194
00:19:47,315 --> 00:19:50,985
Maybe this will always be a part of me.

195
00:19:55,018 --> 00:19:58,897
Hello, Alys, please!
Answer the phone!

196
00:20:01,741 --> 00:20:05,703
But I won’t let it define my life.

197
00:20:06,514 --> 00:20:09,825
I want to live differently now.

198
00:20:09,833 --> 00:20:11,503
Alys.

199
00:20:12,504 --> 00:20:14,006
Pick up!

200
00:20:18,026 --> 00:20:20,779
Not to escape the past,

201
00:20:21,321 --> 00:20:24,199
but to learn how to live with it.

202
00:20:25,103 --> 00:20:28,270
I don't know what's waiting for me there.

203
00:20:29,747 --> 00:20:31,624
But I'm ready to face it.

204
00:20:32,248 --> 00:20:33,541
Okay, thank you.

205
00:20:33,917 --> 00:20:36,122
Dane? Did you reach her yet?

206
00:20:36,130 --> 00:20:38,171
Not yet. Her phone's turned off.

207
00:20:39,005 --> 00:20:41,132
She won't even reply
to any of my messages.

208
00:20:42,133 --> 00:20:44,135
I asked all our relatives.
They had no idea.

209
00:20:44,719 --> 00:20:45,905
I even asked Aya.

210
00:20:45,929 --> 00:20:47,722
We came by Alys' condo earlier.

211
00:20:47,722 --> 00:20:48,722
And?

212
00:20:49,140 --> 00:20:50,140
She's not there.

213
00:20:51,453 --> 00:20:52,871
Her closet's emptied out.

214
00:20:52,874 --> 00:20:54,622
So it means she left?

215
00:20:55,648 --> 00:20:57,441
I mean, didn’t she say
anything to anyone?

216
00:20:57,441 --> 00:20:59,421
Or tell anyone where she's going?

217
00:20:59,429 --> 00:21:01,931
Why would she leave
without telling anyone?

218
00:21:02,335 --> 00:21:04,087
Maybe, Drake?

219
00:21:04,523 --> 00:21:05,828
God, I still hate him.

220
00:21:05,843 --> 00:21:07,166
Ah, Drake!

221
00:21:09,034 --> 00:21:11,370
- Oh, Drake!
- Is Alys here?

222
00:21:11,380 --> 00:21:13,177
She's not at her condo.

223
00:21:13,184 --> 00:21:14,828
We've been looking for her too.

224
00:21:16,217 --> 00:21:17,844
We were about to ask you that.

225
00:21:19,992 --> 00:21:21,077
Alys...

226
00:21:22,083 --> 00:21:23,501
Where did you go?

227
00:21:40,476 --> 00:21:43,396
New country, new air.

228
00:21:43,396 --> 00:21:46,774
No one knows me here.

229
00:21:47,419 --> 00:21:50,464
I hope I find Tripp here.

230
00:22:09,458 --> 00:22:12,169
But can I truly live on my own?

231
00:22:12,169 --> 00:22:14,088
Without relying on anyone?

232
00:22:16,333 --> 00:22:17,793
I can.

233
00:22:17,793 --> 00:22:19,461
You can, Alys.

234
00:22:20,216 --> 00:22:21,634
You can do this.

235
00:22:56,804 --> 00:22:59,890
I have to do this.

236
00:23:31,123 --> 00:23:33,458
So, you're applying as a waitress?

237
00:23:33,842 --> 00:23:35,260
Do you have any experience?

238
00:23:35,700 --> 00:23:36,700
Yes.

239
00:23:37,453 --> 00:23:39,288
I used to run my own pastry shop.

240
00:23:40,493 --> 00:23:42,620
Then why apply as a waitress?

241
00:23:45,114 --> 00:23:47,075
I just wanna start simple.

242
00:24:00,528 --> 00:24:01,822
Hello?

243
00:24:01,833 --> 00:24:04,044
Yeah, yeah!
Do you know where Alys is?

244
00:24:05,559 --> 00:24:07,228
Please give us an update, okay?

245
00:24:07,228 --> 00:24:08,979
Because I'm so worried about her.

246
00:24:09,563 --> 00:24:11,415
Yeah, sorry to bother you.

247
00:24:11,434 --> 00:24:12,978
But do you know where Alys is?

248
00:24:13,716 --> 00:24:16,535
Oh, okay.
Thank you.

249
00:24:16,544 --> 00:24:19,048
Is there any chance

250
00:24:19,052 --> 00:24:21,132
you've seen Alys there in New York?

251
00:24:21,650 --> 00:24:22,650
Hello, Harper?

252
00:24:23,259 --> 00:24:25,613
Yeah, have you seen Alys?

253
00:24:25,637 --> 00:24:27,502
It's been three months.

254
00:24:27,526 --> 00:24:29,121
Please update me, okay?

255
00:24:29,145 --> 00:24:30,730
Alright, bye!

256
00:24:39,066 --> 00:24:40,252
Good morning, Tommy.

257
00:24:40,276 --> 00:24:41,820
Good morning, Alys.

258
00:24:51,164 --> 00:24:51,873
Hello?

259
00:24:54,707 --> 00:24:55,417
Mom!

260
00:24:56,099 --> 00:24:57,170
Alys...

261
00:24:58,044 --> 00:24:59,688
Where are you?

262
00:24:59,712 --> 00:25:02,048
Everybody's worried about you.

263
00:25:02,757 --> 00:25:03,425
I know.

264
00:25:04,905 --> 00:25:06,698
I'm sorry I made you worry, Mom.

265
00:25:07,516 --> 00:25:09,268
But please don't worry about me.

266
00:25:10,306 --> 00:25:11,516
I'm okay.

267
00:25:12,934 --> 00:25:14,394
Where are you, Alys?

268
00:25:15,386 --> 00:25:17,012
California.

269
00:25:18,327 --> 00:25:19,161
What?

270
00:25:19,523 --> 00:25:20,983
What are you doing there?

271
00:25:24,220 --> 00:25:25,930
I just —

272
00:25:27,157 --> 00:25:28,908
I just need this, Mom.

273
00:25:28,908 --> 00:25:30,618
Please trust me on this.

274
00:25:30,618 --> 00:25:33,121
I need this for myself.

275
00:25:35,915 --> 00:25:37,750
And Mom...

276
00:25:38,612 --> 00:25:41,240
Can you keep this between
the two of us for now?

277
00:25:42,554 --> 00:25:44,156
And, I promise,

278
00:25:44,163 --> 00:25:46,093
you don't have to worry about me.

279
00:25:46,812 --> 00:25:49,189
I can handle myself.
I'll be okay.

280
00:25:51,030 --> 00:25:53,575
I'll call you.
I'll always update you.

281
00:25:53,950 --> 00:25:55,493
It's a promise.

282
00:25:55,994 --> 00:25:58,163
Okay, I will not tell anyone.

283
00:25:59,233 --> 00:26:01,486
But please Alys,
please call me, okay?

284
00:26:01,486 --> 00:26:03,362
Keep your promise!

285
00:26:05,031 --> 00:26:06,157
I will.

286
00:26:08,004 --> 00:26:09,297
I love you.

287
00:26:10,227 --> 00:26:11,603
I love you so much, Alys.

288
00:26:42,036 --> 00:26:44,371
Alys, I know you need space.

289
00:26:46,003 --> 00:26:48,714
I know you need to
cut me off from your life.

290
00:26:49,309 --> 00:26:52,312
But not knowing where you
are is driving me insane.

291
00:27:02,523 --> 00:27:03,523
Dane!

292
00:27:03,538 --> 00:27:05,714
Don't be overexcited.
I'm still mad at you.

293
00:27:06,511 --> 00:27:08,463
But even if I am mad at you.

294
00:27:08,487 --> 00:27:11,595
I know you're going crazy
not knowing where my sister went.

295
00:27:12,642 --> 00:27:13,727
Has she called?

296
00:27:14,340 --> 00:27:15,883
Yeah, she called mom.

297
00:27:16,318 --> 00:27:18,445
And she doesn’t want mom to tell anyone.

298
00:27:18,905 --> 00:27:19,905
Even Aya.

299
00:27:20,521 --> 00:27:22,074
But of course,

300
00:27:22,085 --> 00:27:23,711
Mom still told me.

301
00:27:24,337 --> 00:27:26,214
Because she knows
people are worried about her.

302
00:27:28,716 --> 00:27:30,009
So, where is she?

303
00:27:30,921 --> 00:27:32,279
California.

304
00:27:32,303 --> 00:27:33,864
Don't you dare follow her.

305
00:27:33,888 --> 00:27:35,014
Give her space, Drake.

306
00:27:38,512 --> 00:27:39,790
Don't worry, Dane.

307
00:27:41,020 --> 00:27:44,065
I won’t do anything that could
put Alys in danger again.

308
00:27:45,112 --> 00:27:46,405
I've learned my lesson.

309
00:27:48,999 --> 00:27:49,999
Okay.

310
00:28:14,608 --> 00:28:15,784
Hi, excuse me.

311
00:28:15,788 --> 00:28:17,786
Oh, hi. How can I help you?

312
00:28:17,804 --> 00:28:19,056
I'm looking for a patient.

313
00:28:19,056 --> 00:28:20,515
His name is Tripp Marco Palma.

314
00:28:20,515 --> 00:28:22,434
I was just wondering if he's admitted here.

315
00:28:22,434 --> 00:28:23,852
Alright, hold on.
Let me check him.

316
00:28:30,421 --> 00:28:33,382
I'm looking for a patient
named Tripp Marco Palma.

317
00:28:39,257 --> 00:28:41,217
I am sorry, ma'am.

318
00:28:41,217 --> 00:28:43,761
We don't have anyone under that name here.

319
00:28:44,757 --> 00:28:46,824
Oh, okay.

320
00:28:46,848 --> 00:28:48,224
Thank you.

321
00:28:59,508 --> 00:29:01,802
I won't stop until I find you, Tripp.

322
00:29:08,429 --> 00:29:10,264
Dear Alys,

323
00:29:18,626 --> 00:29:21,559
I don't know if this
email will ever reach you.

324
00:29:23,457 --> 00:29:25,793
I don’t know if you’ll ever read this.

325
00:29:27,526 --> 00:29:29,403
But I'll write you anyway.

326
00:29:30,622 --> 00:29:31,998
Life's been...

327
00:29:33,190 --> 00:29:34,566
quiet lately.

328
00:30:04,616 --> 00:30:05,659
Morning, Tommy.

329
00:30:05,659 --> 00:30:06,827
Morning, Alys.

330
00:30:09,944 --> 00:30:11,446
Morning, Abby.

331
00:30:11,446 --> 00:30:13,031
Morning, Alys.

332
00:30:16,436 --> 00:30:18,354
Good morning, Kev.

333
00:30:18,354 --> 00:30:20,023
Morning, Alys.

334
00:30:23,610 --> 00:30:27,606
I guess that's what happens
when someone important

335
00:30:27,630 --> 00:30:30,633
disappears from your life.

336
00:30:32,171 --> 00:30:33,380
They said you left.

337
00:30:35,443 --> 00:30:37,655
I don't know where exactly,

338
00:30:37,679 --> 00:30:39,139
but I hope you're okay.

339
00:30:49,710 --> 00:30:50,837
Excuse me.

340
00:30:50,850 --> 00:30:52,463
Yes, ma'am.
How can I help you?

341
00:30:52,463 --> 00:30:55,883
Is there a patient here
named Tripp Marco Palma?

342
00:30:55,890 --> 00:30:57,089
Okay, ma'am.
Wait.

343
00:30:57,113 --> 00:30:58,237
Hold on.

344
00:30:58,261 --> 00:31:01,013
What if he's not here too?

345
00:31:01,988 --> 00:31:03,406
How are you related to the patient?

346
00:31:05,103 --> 00:31:07,523
I hope you find the peace
you are looking for.

347
00:31:15,395 --> 00:31:17,438
You don't need to reply.

348
00:31:17,462 --> 00:31:19,297
I understand if you still don’t want to.

349
00:31:29,015 --> 00:31:30,688
Just know that wherever you go,

350
00:31:32,039 --> 00:31:33,249
I'm still here.

351
00:31:44,514 --> 00:31:46,099
Waiting...

352
00:31:47,417 --> 00:31:49,753
and I’ll continue to wait for you.

353
00:31:53,631 --> 00:31:56,258
Finally, I found you, Tripp.

354
00:32:07,206 --> 00:32:08,332
Hello, Marco.

355
00:32:10,130 --> 00:32:11,882
You were so hard to find.

356
00:32:13,293 --> 00:32:15,754
I had to go all the way here in California.

357
00:32:18,082 --> 00:32:21,043
And you know me, I'm stubborn.

358
00:32:32,091 --> 00:32:35,386
I'll always find you wherever you go.

359
00:32:36,171 --> 00:32:38,465
So please, Tripp.

360
00:32:41,128 --> 00:32:43,214
Wake up.

361
00:32:45,531 --> 00:32:48,033
I’m never leaving again, I promise.

362
00:32:50,704 --> 00:32:53,081
I won't leave until you wake up.

363
00:32:58,954 --> 00:33:01,331
I’m so sorry.

364
00:33:06,927 --> 00:33:09,013
I’m so sorry.

365
00:33:27,046 --> 00:33:28,973
Three years have passed,

366
00:33:28,983 --> 00:33:30,985
and this is my life now.

367
00:33:31,460 --> 00:33:34,338
Still working as a waitress
in this small cafe.

368
00:33:34,811 --> 00:33:38,398
And in this country, I am a nobody.

369
00:33:40,150 --> 00:33:41,985
Thank you for coming. See us again!

370
00:33:45,864 --> 00:33:47,574
Hey, I got this.

371
00:33:48,046 --> 00:33:49,423
- You sure?
- Yeah, for sure.

372
00:33:49,423 --> 00:33:50,733
Please take a break.

373
00:33:50,757 --> 00:33:52,509
Thanks. See you in fifteen.

374
00:33:52,515 --> 00:33:53,599
Okay, sounds good.

375
00:33:54,211 --> 00:33:57,381
But surprisingly, it feels good.

376
00:33:58,007 --> 00:34:00,551
No pressure, no stress.

377
00:34:06,163 --> 00:34:08,040
705 emails.

378
00:34:08,801 --> 00:34:10,594
That madman hasn't stopped.

379
00:34:16,989 --> 00:34:17,990
Hi, Alys.

380
00:34:18,929 --> 00:34:19,929
How are you?

381
00:34:21,038 --> 00:34:22,289
We're doing fine here.

382
00:34:22,843 --> 00:34:25,095
Your Mom and the others are doing well.

383
00:34:26,124 --> 00:34:29,616
And Dane, he's still angry with me.

384
00:34:30,022 --> 00:34:31,045
But that's okay.

385
00:34:36,623 --> 00:34:40,836
Anyway, I made a tiny altar
in memory of Marco.

386
00:34:41,693 --> 00:34:43,945
Why did you name him Marco?

387
00:34:46,023 --> 00:34:47,858
Tripp's still alive, isn't he?

388
00:34:48,802 --> 00:34:49,802
But fine.

389
00:34:51,127 --> 00:34:52,545
I won't question it.

390
00:34:53,513 --> 00:34:55,974
Because you're Marco's mother.

391
00:35:18,191 --> 00:35:22,278
3 years, 765 emails.

392
00:35:22,287 --> 00:35:23,455
Zero reply.

393
00:35:24,062 --> 00:35:25,819
They told me, “Give up, Drake.”

394
00:35:26,537 --> 00:35:27,537
She's moved on.

395
00:35:28,484 --> 00:35:29,693
But hell, I won't.

396
00:35:30,731 --> 00:35:32,774
You haven't forgotten about me, right?

397
00:35:33,425 --> 00:35:35,261
You said you love me.

398
00:35:35,713 --> 00:35:37,256
You just need a break.

399
00:35:38,269 --> 00:35:39,562
I wish you were here.

400
00:35:40,653 --> 00:35:41,862
I love you.

401
00:35:42,224 --> 00:35:43,517
I still do.

402
00:35:44,419 --> 00:35:45,734
And I will always.

403
00:35:46,729 --> 00:35:48,564
You said you love me.

404
00:35:49,143 --> 00:35:51,072
I'm holding you to that, Alys.

405
00:35:52,436 --> 00:35:53,436
Hi, Abby.

406
00:35:53,451 --> 00:35:54,451
Hi, Alys.

407
00:35:55,022 --> 00:35:56,106
Hi, Kevz.

408
00:35:56,565 --> 00:35:58,025
- Hi, Tommy.
- Hi, Alys.

409
00:35:58,442 --> 00:35:59,443
Hello, you.

410
00:36:04,654 --> 00:36:08,825
I'd rather die than
replace you in my life.

411
00:36:10,023 --> 00:36:12,067
You can call me a fool, Alys.

412
00:36:12,927 --> 00:36:14,679
If you ever find someone new,

413
00:36:15,673 --> 00:36:17,800
don't invite me to your wedding, okay?

414
00:36:18,960 --> 00:36:20,711
Or don't marry at all.

415
00:36:22,026 --> 00:36:24,445
You're still married, remember?

416
00:36:26,435 --> 00:36:27,812
I love you, Alys.

417
00:36:29,247 --> 00:36:30,247
Always.

418
00:36:31,367 --> 00:36:32,367
Drake.

419
00:36:32,375 --> 00:36:33,727
Hi, my name is Alys.

420
00:36:33,742 --> 00:36:34,994
What can I get for you today?

421
00:36:38,581 --> 00:36:39,898
- Go ahead, Tommy.
- Okay.

422
00:36:39,906 --> 00:36:40,906
Bye, Alys.

423
00:36:47,371 --> 00:36:48,664
Are you okay, Alys?

424
00:36:49,227 --> 00:36:50,227
What?

425
00:36:50,917 --> 00:36:52,919
Yeah, I'm fine.
I just got distracted.

426
00:36:53,622 --> 00:36:54,622
Okay.

427
00:37:04,514 --> 00:37:05,514
Hey, Tommy.

428
00:37:06,216 --> 00:37:07,467
Don't you have a date tonight?

429
00:37:08,032 --> 00:37:09,032
Yeah.

430
00:37:10,931 --> 00:37:12,433
Well, go on.

431
00:37:12,815 --> 00:37:14,083
I'll close the shop for you.

432
00:37:14,107 --> 00:37:15,316
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

433
00:37:15,316 --> 00:37:17,836
Don't you need to visit
your friend at the hospital?

434
00:37:17,844 --> 00:37:19,610
I will, but after this.

435
00:37:19,625 --> 00:37:22,323
I'm not in a rush anyway,
so just go ahead.

436
00:37:22,323 --> 00:37:23,991
Okay. Thank you so much.

437
00:37:23,991 --> 00:37:25,234
You're the best.

438
00:37:25,242 --> 00:37:26,660
- You owe me one.
- Okay.

439
00:37:43,406 --> 00:37:44,740
I love you, Alys.

440
00:37:46,223 --> 00:37:47,223
Always.

441
00:37:48,427 --> 00:37:49,427
Drake.

442
00:38:00,600 --> 00:38:02,060
I'm not mad.

443
00:38:02,983 --> 00:38:05,152
I just needed space to rebuild my life.

444
00:38:06,857 --> 00:38:08,919
I'm done loving someone too much.

445
00:38:10,537 --> 00:38:12,748
When you love someone too much,

446
00:38:13,332 --> 00:38:15,542
you leave nothing for yourself.

447
00:38:16,252 --> 00:38:18,295
What if they leave you?

448
00:38:18,295 --> 00:38:19,964
Then you lose everything.

449
00:38:22,844 --> 00:38:26,264
And I promised Tripp.

450
00:38:27,395 --> 00:38:31,066
I'm not going home until he wakes up.

451
00:38:45,296 --> 00:38:46,672
Hello, Silly.

452
00:38:48,601 --> 00:38:50,186
Can you give me a smile?

453
00:38:51,859 --> 00:38:53,861
I had a boring day at work.

454
00:38:53,861 --> 00:38:55,154
Nothing really happened.

455
00:39:00,135 --> 00:39:01,929
Wake up, please?

456
00:39:02,544 --> 00:39:05,255
You know, I've gotten really
good at making coffee.

457
00:39:05,794 --> 00:39:07,004
I'll make you some.

458
00:39:10,304 --> 00:39:12,473
You won't be able to drink it, though.

459
00:39:14,446 --> 00:39:16,031
Smell it instead.

460
00:39:35,876 --> 00:39:37,419
Hello, Marco.

461
00:39:38,430 --> 00:39:39,682
I’m sorry.

462
00:39:39,682 --> 00:39:42,017
I can only visit twice a month now.

463
00:39:43,244 --> 00:39:45,955
I’m working two shifts now.

464
00:39:48,013 --> 00:39:49,639
Anyway, are you ready?

465
00:39:55,211 --> 00:39:58,172
Once upon a time, there was a man who used

466
00:39:58,172 --> 00:40:00,711
to love chasing sunsets.

467
00:40:00,719 --> 00:40:04,469
He searched far and wide for
the most beautiful sunset but

468
00:40:05,176 --> 00:40:07,053
he couldn't seem to find it.

469
00:40:09,058 --> 00:40:16,899
[singing] Happy birthday to you.

470
00:40:17,803 --> 00:40:21,849
[singing] Happy birthday, happy birthday.

471
00:40:26,629 --> 00:40:29,674
[singing] Happy birthday to you.

472
00:40:52,700 --> 00:40:54,869
I wish...

473
00:40:56,318 --> 00:40:59,404
you'd wake up already.

474
00:41:05,770 --> 00:41:08,565
I'll be back next week, okay?

475
00:41:10,199 --> 00:41:12,576
I love you, Marco.

476
00:41:34,633 --> 00:41:36,510
Where’s Tripp?

477
00:41:38,547 --> 00:41:39,625
Excuse me.

478
00:41:39,625 --> 00:41:41,714
Are you looking for Mr. Palma?

479
00:41:41,727 --> 00:41:42,813
Yes.

480
00:41:42,820 --> 00:41:45,340
Did his mother transfer him
to a different hospital again?

481
00:41:45,344 --> 00:41:46,750
She always does that.

482
00:41:46,758 --> 00:41:47,929
His mom picked him up.

483
00:41:48,972 --> 00:41:49,639
Oh my God.

484
00:41:49,649 --> 00:41:52,765
Where have you gone now,
Tripp Marco Palma?

485
00:41:52,766 --> 00:41:54,186
Excuse me, ma'am.

486
00:41:54,188 --> 00:41:56,480
No, he was discharged two weeks ago.

487
00:41:57,727 --> 00:41:58,727
Discharged?

488
00:41:58,734 --> 00:42:01,484
Yes, he's been responsive
for a few months now.

489
00:42:02,290 --> 00:42:04,542
He could hear, he could feel.

490
00:42:04,542 --> 00:42:07,628
We were surprised that
he finally woke up now.

491
00:42:08,710 --> 00:42:09,961
Excuse me, ma'am.

492
00:42:15,810 --> 00:42:16,810
Tripp.

493
00:42:43,033 --> 00:42:47,364
[singing] Happy birthday to you.

494
00:42:47,375 --> 00:42:51,727
[singing] Happy birthday to you.

495
00:42:51,734 --> 00:42:55,759
[singing] Happy birthday, happy birthday.

496
00:43:00,537 --> 00:43:03,790
[singing] Happy birthday to you.

497
00:43:26,576 --> 00:43:28,536
I wish...

498
00:43:30,322 --> 00:43:33,033
you'd wake up already.

499
00:43:39,714 --> 00:43:41,758
I'll be back next week, okay?

500
00:43:44,155 --> 00:43:45,699
I love you, Marco.

501
00:44:28,143 --> 00:44:30,562
I know a place where
you can get Adobo.

502
00:44:31,719 --> 00:44:35,139
On the last episode of
Dating Alys Perez.

503
00:44:43,116 --> 00:44:44,701
Hi, sir. How may I help you?

504
00:44:52,428 --> 00:44:53,429
Zy!

505
00:44:56,076 --> 00:44:57,234
You did nothing wrong.

506
00:44:58,506 --> 00:45:00,080
I have never blamed you.

507
00:45:00,675 --> 00:45:02,344
I am not blaming you.

508
00:45:02,344 --> 00:45:03,428
I will never blame you.

509
00:45:03,887 --> 00:45:05,096
I'm coming home to you.

510
00:45:06,702 --> 00:45:07,703
Turn around.
